{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794532152059,"sessionID":"ses_e2d8e593affeqxRun8M4iooLPr","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2739142001e6S8c4s1q278De","sessionID":"ses_e2d8e593affeqxRun8M4iooLPr","messageID":"msg_1d2738050001jkzR6J2PGUa3Tl","type":"tool","id":"call_1f570460f3034d0a932452b8","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/tasks.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/tasks.md, lines 1-222\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Tasks: Phase 6: gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers\"\n3: description: \"Ordered tasks to add the Gate 2 command bullet, copy it into the Cursor rule, hand hub modes to their commands, name the plan workflow at Gate 3 and downgrade commands in a child brief.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"gate 2 binding and runtime pointers tasks\"\n6: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7: contextType: \"general\"\n8: ---\n9: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n10: # Tasks: Phase 6: gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers\n11: \n12: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n17: ## Task Notation\n18: \n19: | Prefix | Meaning |\n20: |--------|---------|\n21: | `[ ]` | Pending |\n22: | `[x]` | Completed |\n23: | `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n24: | `[B]` | Blocked |\n25: \n26: **Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n27: \n28: Every command runs from the repository root unless a task says otherwise. `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`. `SSK` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime`. `SYNC` is `$SSK/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs`. `MAN` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json`. `CHK` is `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs`. `HOOKDOC` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`. `S` is this phase's `scratch/` folder. `G1T` is `(cd $SSK/cli && npx vitest run tests/gate1-pointer-sync.vitest.ts --config ../vitest.config.ts --root .)`.\n29: \n30: Each task is one change to the files it names, small enough for a worker with a short brief. The operator answered the four wording questions on 2026-11-12, and `spec.md` section 10 quotes each answer. No task reads holdout prompt text.\n31: \n32: Worker waves. Tasks in one wave touch different files and can run in parallel.\n33: - Wave 0, 2 tasks: T001, T002. Read-only setup.\n34: - Wave 1, 12 tasks: T003 (`AGENTS.md`), T004 (`SYNC`), T005 (`HOOKDOC`), T006 (`advisor-runtime-values.ts`), T007 (`advisor-observability.vitest.ts`), T008 (`hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts`), T009, T010 and T011 (one `ROUTER.md` each), T012 (`spec-gate-core.mjs`), T013 (`create.sh`), T014 (the deriver, only if its condition holds).\n35: - Wave 2, 8 tasks: T015 (`render.ts`), T016 (`MAN`), T017 (gate1 test), T018 (`HOOKDOC`), T019 (parity test, new), T020 (spec-gate test), T021 (runtime-mirrors README), T022 (label removal test, new).\n36: - Wave 3, 4 tasks: T023 (child render test, new), T024 (`MAN`, generated), T025 (`.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md`, generated), T026 (`HOOKDOC`).\n37: - Verification, 9 tasks, one at a time: T027 to T035.\n38: <!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n39: \n40: ---\n41: \n42: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n43: ## Phase 1: Setup\n44: \n45: - [x] T001 Re-read the before numbers (`$S/before.txt`). Verify: `$CHK | grep -E \"^A(4|6) |^STATUS\"` prints `44 current`, `15629 of 16384` and `STATUS=OK`, `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-manifest.cjs --check` prints `30 pins`, `node $SYNC --check` exits 0 and `node $S/measure-policies.mjs | head -1` prints `commands 44 {\"start\":20,\"ask\":17,\"run\":7}`.\n46: - [x] T002 Confirm phase 005 shipped the brief line (`$S/phase005-check.txt`). Verify: `bash $S/hook-first-line.sh \"create a readme for the utils folder\"` prints a line holding `/create:readme` and `(start)`. If it does not, mark T014, T015, T023, T026 and T033 `[B]` with the line it printed, and carry on with the rest.\n47: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n48: \n49: ---\n50: \n51: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n52: ## Phase 2: Implementation\n53: \n54: - [x] T003 Insert one line in `AGENTS.md` Gate 2, right after the line `- Confidence ≥ 0.8 → MUST invoke skill | < 0.8 → general approach | User names skill → cite and proceed`. The line is the exact content of `$S/bullet-draft.txt`: ``- **Command in the brief.** A brief or advisor result that names a command offers its workflow beside the skill's. Take either path whole, never an improvised one. To take the command, read its document in full and follow it. `run` starts it now. `start` starts it without `:auto`, so its setup asks. `ask` offers it in one question and waits. A typed command or explicit instruction outranks the policy. Output: `COMMAND: [/name] → [started|offered|declined]` `` (`AGENTS.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"^- \\*\\*Command in the brief\\.\\*\\*\" AGENTS.md` prints 1, and `diff <(rg \"^- \\*\\*Command in the brief\" AGENTS.md) $S/bullet-draft.txt` prints nothing.\n55: - [x] T004 In `SYNC`, add a second block. Add the constants `START_COMMAND = '<!-- spec-kit:gate2-command-pointer:start -->'`, `END_COMMAND = '<!-- spec-kit:gate2-command-pointer:end -->'`, `GATE_TWO_CALL_MARKER = 'skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend'` and `GATE_TWO_COMMAND_MARKER = '**Command in the brief.**'`. Read the first `AGENTS.md` line holding each marker, with a leading `2. ` stripped as `readGateOneLine` does. When both lines exist, write a block right after the Gate 1 block: the start marker, `## Gate 2 command routing (generated from the root AGENTS.md)`, a blank line, `Cursor gets no per-prompt advisor brief under the tested build. Before acting, run the direct call below, then apply the command rule:`, a blank line, the call line, a blank line, the command line, a blank line, the same `Generated by` line as block one, the end marker. When either line is missing, remove an existing second block and write nothing for it. Under `--check`, report `pointer block differs from the root AGENTS.md Gate 2 lines` or `no Gate 2 command block` and exit 1. Export the new names (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs`). Verify: `node --check $SYNC` exits 0, and `rg -c \"GATE_TWO_COMMAND_MARKER = '\\*\\*Command in the brief\\.\\*\\*'\" $SYNC` prints 1.\n56: - [x] T005 [P] In `HOOKDOC` section 3, add a DSH row after the OpenCode row: runtime `**DSH**`, adapter `system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs`, imported by `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/prompt-advisor.mjs`, wiring `agent/pre-step` through the `repo-guards` plugin, on unless the `promptAdvisor` row flag is `false`, payload note `A fan-out leaf, marked by the lineage patch, gets no brief`, delivery `Brief added to the step`. In section 4, add a `dsh/` entry with `README.md` and `prompt-advisor.mjs` (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`). Verify: `rg -n '^\\| \\*\\*DSH\\*\\* \\|' $HOOKDOC` prints 1 line, and `rg -c \"prompt-advisor.mjs\" $HOOKDOC` prints at least 2.\n57: - [x] T006 [P] Remove the `'copilot',` line from `ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES`, leaving seven labels in this order: `claude`, `opencode`, `pi`, `codex`, `cursor`, `devin`, `dsh`. Add no retired list (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/advisor-runtime-values.ts`). Verify: `rg -c \"copilot\" $ADV/lib/advisor-runtime-values.ts` prints nothing and exits 1, and in `$ADV`, `npm run typecheck` exits 0.\n58: - [x] T007 [P] In the observability test, change the expectation `expect(ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES).toEqual([...])` to the seven labels T006 leaves, in the same order (`$ADV/tests/legacy/advisor-observability.vitest.ts`). Verify: after T006, in `$ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/legacy/advisor-observability.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, and `rg -c \"copilot\" $ADV/tests/legacy/advisor-observability.vitest.ts` prints nothing.\n59: - [x] T008 [P] In the brief benchmark, delete the `copilot` row of `SEVEN_AXIS_MATRIX` and drop `copilot` from the header comment that lists the runtimes (`$ADV/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts`). Verify: `rg -c \"copilot\" $ADV/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts` prints nothing and exits 1. The bench sits outside `npm run typecheck` and the default test run, so this grep is its check.\n60: - [x] T009 [P] Add one bullet as the last item of section 4, HOW TO READ THIS, in `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md`: ``- A mode whose `mode-registry.json` row names a `command` has two whole entries: read that command's document in full and follow it under the policy the advisor names, or follow this mode's packet. Pick one and keep to it. A mode whose row has `command: null` has only its packet.`` (`.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"has two whole entries\" .skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md` prints 1, and `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/sk-doc` exits 0.\n61: - [x] T010 [P] Add the same bullet as T009 as the last item of section 4 in `.skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md` (`.skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"has two whole entries\" .skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md` prints 1, and `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/sk-design` exits 0.\n62: - [x] T011 [P] Add the T009 bullet as the last item of section 4 in `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/ROUTER.md`, followed in the same bullet by: ``Where a mode packet names its command as its only entry, as `deep-research/SKILL.md` does, both entries lead to the command.`` (`.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/ROUTER.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"has two whole entries\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/ROUTER.md` prints 1, and `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop` exits 0.\n63: - [x] T012 [P] In `GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE`, insert one array item right after `'The answer holds for the rest of this session: do not ask this again on later turns.'`: `'For a new folder, start /speckit:plan, or /speckit:complete when the operator asked for the build itself: read that command document in full and follow it without :auto.'` (`$SSK/hooks/lib/spec-gate/spec-gate-core.mjs`). Verify: `rg -c \"speckit:plan\" $SSK/hooks/lib/spec-gate/spec-gate-core.mjs` prints 1, and `node --check $SSK/hooks/lib/spec-gate/spec-gate-core.mjs` exits 0.\n64: - [x] T013 [P] In the standard next-steps block of `create.sh`, the one that prints `1. Fill out spec.md with requirements`, add after the lazy add-ons `if` block: `echo \"    6. Plan the work with /speckit:plan, or plan and build with /speckit:complete, unless one of them created this folder\"` (`$SSK/cli/spec/create.sh`). Verify: `bash -n $SSK/cli/spec/create.sh` exits 0, and `rg -c \"6. Plan the work with /speckit:plan\" $SSK/cli/spec/create.sh` prints 1.\n65: - [x] T014 The command table phase 005 generates (`COMMAND_ROWS` in `$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`) carries a policy but no `mutating` class, and T015 needs the class. In `renderCommandRows` of `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs`, add `mutating: '<class>'` to each `COMMAND_ROWS` row, taken from the same `commandPolicies` record that supplies the row's policy, placed after `policy` and left out when the row has no policy record. In `$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`, add `readonly mutating?: 'read-only' | 'add-only' | 'mutates';` to the `CommandRow` interface, outside the generated block. Then run `node $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs`. Verify: `node $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs --check | jq -r .status` prints `fresh`, `rg -c \"'command-doctor-git-setup': \\{ command: '/doctor:git setup', policy: 'run', mutating: 'read-only'\" $ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` prints 1, `rg -c \"'command-doctor-speckit': \\{ command: '/doctor:speckit', policy: 'run', mutating: 'add-only'\" $ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` prints 1, and in `$ADV`, `npm run typecheck` exits 0 and `npx vitest run tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts tests/doctor-command-bridges.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n66: - [ ] T015 In `$ADV/lib/render.ts`, add `childSession?: boolean` to `AdvisorBriefRenderOptions`, defaulting to `process.env.AI_SESSION_CHILD === '1'`. When it is true, the command shown in the head line, and in an `Also:` line, renders `(parent-named only)` in place of its policy word when the policy is `start` or `ask`, or when it is `run` and the class is not `read-only`. Nothing else in the brief changes (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV`, `npm run typecheck` exits 0, and `npx vitest run tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts tests/hooks` reports 0 failed.\n67: - [ ] T016 [P] In `MAN` `pins`, add an entry right after `gate1-lookup`: `\"id\": \"gate2-command\"`, `\"kind\": \"first-occurrence\"`, `\"section\": \"gate-2\"`, `\"texts\": [\"**Command in the brief.**\"]`, `\"consumer\": \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs\"`, `\"consumer_evidence\": [\"GATE_TWO_COMMAND_MARKER = '**Command in the brief.**'\"]` and a `why` saying the Cursor rule's second block is generated from the first line holding this marker (`.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json`). Verify: `node -e 'const m=require(\"./.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json\");console.log(m.pins.length, m.pins.some((p)=>p.id===\"gate2-command\"))'` prints `31 true`.\n68: - [ ] T017 [P] In `gate1-pointer-sync.vitest.ts`, seed `AGENTS.md` with a Gate 2 call line and a command line, and add three cases: both blocks are written and `--check` exits 0, a root with no command line gets block one only and a stale second block is removed, and a hand edit inside the second block makes `--check` exit 1 with `pointer block differs from the root AGENTS.md Gate 2 lines` (`$SSK/cli/tests/gate1-pointer-sync.vitest.ts`). Verify: `$G1T` reports 7 passed and 0 failed.\n69: - [ ] T018 [P] In `HOOKDOC`, add a subsection `### Starting a surfaced command` at the end of section 3. It says the command document is `.skilled/commands/<group>/<name>.md`, the model reads it in full and follows it on every runtime, never tells the user to type a slash command and asks the user to type one only when it cannot read the file. Then a table with columns `Runtime`, `Model can start a command itself` and `Basis`, one row each for Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Devin, Pi, OpenCode and DSH, taken from section 2.8 of `../../007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/synthesis-review.md`. Write runtime names in plain text, not bold, so the parity test reads only the adapter table. Claude Code's row says the Skill tool is a shortcut for the names it lists, and that it lists one `create` entry and none of the other twelve `create:*` names (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`). Verify: `rg -n \"^### Starting a surfaced command\" $HOOKDOC` prints 1 line, and `rg -c '^\\| \\*\\*' $HOOKDOC` still prints 7.\n70: - [ ] T019 [P] Create `$ADV/tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts`. Export a pure `compareRuntimeLists(index, table, enumValues)` that returns the names missing from each list. Read the index as the directory names under `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/`, the table as the lowercased bold names in `HOOKDOC` rows matching `^\\| \\*\\*([A-Za-z]+)\\*\\* \\|`, and the enum as `ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES`. One case asserts the three real lists agree. One case passes an index with an extra name and asserts the function reports it (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts` reports 2 passed and 0 failed.\n71: - [ ] T020 [P] In the test `Gate-3 delivery flag off preserves byte-identical baseline output`, add the T012 line to the `mutationNotice` array at the same position (`$SSK/tests/hooks/spec-gate-core.test.mjs`). Verify: `(cd $SSK && node --test tests/hooks/spec-gate-core.test.mjs)` prints `fail 0` and `pass 107`.\n72: - [ ] T021 [P] In the `sync-gate1-pointers.cjs` row of the runtime-mirrors README, say the script writes two blocks into `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md`: the Gate 1 lookup and the Gate 2 command rule with its direct call (`$SSK/cli/runtime-mirrors/README.md`). Verify: `rg -n \"sync-gate1-pointers\" $SSK/cli/runtime-mirrors/README.md` prints a line naming `Gate 2`.\n73: - [ ] T022 [P] Create `$ADV/tests/legacy/runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts` for a record or input that still carries `copilot`. Use a temporary workspace root and delete the two files it writes afterwards. Cases: a diagnostics file at `advisorHookDiagnosticsPath(root)` holding one valid `claude` record and one otherwise valid `copilot` record makes `readAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecords(root)` return only the `claude` record without throwing. The same holds for an outcomes file at `advisorHookOutcomesPath(root)` and `readAdvisorHookOutcomeRecords(root)`. `serializeAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord` throws for a `copilot` record. `validateSkillExecutionOutcomeRecord` returns false for one. `AdvisorValidateInputSchema.safeParse` fails for an `outcomeEvents` entry with `runtime: 'copilot'` and names that path in its issues (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/legacy/runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts`). Verify: after T006, in `$ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/legacy/runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts` reports 5 passed and 0 failed.\n74: - [ ] T023 [P] Create `$ADV/tests/render-child-session.vitest.ts`. Cases, each rendering one result through `renderAdvisorBrief`: child set and policy `start`, `ask`, `run` with `read-only` and `run` with `add-only`, then the variable set to `0` and unset. Expected: `(parent-named only)` for `start`, `ask` and `run` with `add-only`, the policy word for `run` with `read-only`, and output byte-equal to the non-child render for `0` and unset. One more case renders `/doctor:git hooks` as top with the child set (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/render-child-session.vitest.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/render-child-session.vitest.ts` reports 7 passed and 0 failed.\n75: - [ ] T024 Regenerate the manifest's derived copy (`MAN`). Verify: `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-manifest.cjs --write` exits 0, then `--check` prints `PASS: 44 sections, 31 pins, derived matches AGENTS.md`.\n76: - [ ] T025 [P] Regenerate the Cursor rule (`.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md`). Verify: `node $SYNC` exits 0, then `node $SYNC --check` exits 0, `rg -c \"Command in the brief\" .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` prints 1 and `rg -c \"skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend\" .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` prints 1.\n77: - [ ] T026 [P] In `HOOKDOC` section 2, step 5 Render, add one sentence: with `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` a surfaced `start` or `ask` command, or a `run` command that is not read-only, renders as `(parent-named only)` (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"parent-named only\" $HOOKDOC` prints 1.\n78: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n79: \n80: ---\n81: \n82: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n83: ## Phase 3: Verification\n84: \n85: - [ ] T027 Run the agents-md check (`$S/after-check.txt`). Verify: `$CHK` prints `STATUS=OK`, A4 `44 current`, A5 `31/31 pins hold`, A10 `6/6` and A6 at or under `16384`, expected `16092` with the T003 text unchanged.\n86: - [ ] T028 Run the rule-copy canary. Verify: `node .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/scripts/check-rule-copies.js | head -1` prints a line starting `OK: all rule invariants present`.\n87: - [ ] T029 Run the pointer test and check. Verify: `$G1T` reports 7 passed, and `node $SYNC --check` exits 0.\n88: - [ ] T030 Run the spec gate test. Verify: `(cd $SSK && node --test tests/hooks/spec-gate-core.test.mjs)` prints `fail 0`.\n89: - [ ] T031 Run the advisor checks. Verify: in `$ADV`, `npm run typecheck` exits 0, `npx vitest run tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts tests/render-child-session.vitest.ts tests/legacy/runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts tests/legacy/advisor-observability.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `rg -n \"copilot\" $ADV --glob \"*.ts\" --glob \"!dist/**\" --glob \"!node_modules/**\"` prints only the new test and the adapter-path guards in `tests/hooks/settings-driven-invocation-parity.vitest.ts` and `stress-test/skill-advisor/hooks-parity-stress.vitest.ts` and `npm test` reports 0 failed.\n90: - [ ] T032 Run the three hub checks. Verify: `for h in sk-doc sk-design system-deep-loop; do node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/$h > /dev/null 2>&1; echo \"$h exit=$?\"; done` prints `exit=0` three times.\n91: - [ ] T033 Rebuild the advisor and probe the hook. Verify: in `$ADV`, `npm run build` exits 0. Then `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1 bash $S/hook-first-line.sh \"disable comment hygiene gate\"` prints a line holding `/doctor:git hooks (parent-named only)`, and the same command without the variable prints the phase 005 line with its policy word.\n92: - [ ] T034 Check scope and comment hygiene. Verify: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --stat` names only files in `spec.md` section 3, and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff -U0 -- '*.ts' '*.cjs' '*.mjs' '*.sh' | rg \"^\\+.*(REQ-0|T0[0-9]{2}|specs/|ADR-)\"` prints nothing.\n93: - [ ] T035 Write `implementation-summary.md` and mark each row in `acceptance-criteria.md` with its evidence. Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <this folder> --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n94: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n95: \n96: ---\n97: \n98: <!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n99: ## Completion Criteria\n100: \n101: - [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n102: - [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n103: - [ ] `$CHK` prints `STATUS=OK` and `node $SYNC --check` exits 0 with the bullet in place\n104: <!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n105: \n106: ---\n107: \n108: <!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n109: ## Cross-References\n110: \n111: - **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n112: - **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n113: - **Acceptance criteria**: See `acceptance-criteria.md`\n114: - **Review**: `../../007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/synthesis-review.md` R5, R6, R10b, L4, L5, L10, G1 and G3\n115: <!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n116: \n117: ---\n118: \n119: ## Verification Checklist\n120: \n121: <!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n122: ## Verification Protocol\n123: \n124: | Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n125: |----------|----------|-------------------|\n126: | **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n127: | **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n128: | **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n129: \n130: A blocked task gets `[B]` and one line naming what blocks it. An A6 reading above 16384 blocks the phase.\n131: <!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n132: \n133: ---\n134: \n135: <!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n136: ## Pre-Implementation\n137: \n138: - [x] CHK-001 [P0] The four wording questions have an operator answer, quoted in `spec.md` section 10. Evidence: answered on 2026-11-12 through the question dialog. T003, T006, T012, T013, T015 and T026 follow those answers.\n139: - [ ] CHK-002 [P0] The before numbers are in `$S/before.txt` (T001).\n140: - [ ] CHK-003 [P1] Phase 005's brief line is confirmed, or the REQ-004 tasks are marked `[B]` (T002).\n141: <!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n142: \n143: ---\n144: \n145: <!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n146: ## Code Quality\n147: \n148: - [ ] CHK-010 [P0] In `$ADV`, `npm run typecheck` exits 0, and `node --check` exits 0 on `SYNC` and `spec-gate-core.mjs`.\n149: - [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No code comment names a spec path, a phase number, a requirement or a task id (T034).\n150: - [ ] CHK-012 [P1] `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` is written by `SYNC` only, never by hand (T025).\n151: - [ ] CHK-013 [P1] The child branch reads the class, never the policy word alone (T015, T023).\n152: <!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n153: \n154: ---\n155: \n156: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n157: ## Testing Checklist\n158: \n159: - [ ] CHK-020 [P0] `$CHK` prints `STATUS=OK` with A6 at or under 16384 (T027).\n160: - [ ] CHK-021 [P0] The pointer test passes 7 cases and `--check` exits 0 (T029).\n161: - [ ] CHK-022 [P0] The child render test covers every renderer axis in `plan.md` (T023).\n162: - [ ] CHK-023 [P1] The spec gate test, the parity test and `npm test` in `$ADV` report 0 failed (T030, T031).\n163: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n164: \n165: ---\n166: \n167: <!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n168: ## FIX ADDENDUM: FIX COMPLETENESS\n169: \n170: - [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] The gap is class `cross-consumer`: one rule, read by seven runtimes through four surfaces.\n171: - [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Every reader of the pointer generator is checked: `rg -l \"sync-gate1-pointers\" .skilled --glob '!**/node_modules/**' --glob '!**/dist/**'` lists only files this phase changed or confirmed unchanged in `plan.md`.\n172: - [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Every reader of `GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE` is checked: `rg -n \"GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE\" .skilled --glob '!**/dist/**'` lists the core, its test and the injection contract, which names it without quoting it.\n173: - [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P1] The matrix axes in `plan.md` are listed in the two test file headers.\n174: - [ ] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] The child test sets and restores `AI_SESSION_CHILD`, so no other test sees it.\n175: - [ ] CHK-FIX-006 [P1] Evidence names the commit it ran on.\n176: <!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n177: \n178: ---\n179: \n180: <!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n181: ## Security\n182: \n183: - [ ] CHK-030 [P0] A child never sees a bare `start` or `ask` command line (T023).\n184: - [ ] CHK-031 [P0] No changed file names `/local-skilled-alignment`: `rg -n \"local-skilled-alignment\" <changed files>` prints nothing.\n185: - [ ] CHK-032 [P1] The pointer block copies tracked `AGENTS.md` text only (T004).\n186: - [ ] CHK-033 [P0] A stored record carrying `copilot` is skipped by both readers without an error, and tool input carrying it is rejected (T022).\n187: <!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n188: \n189: ---\n190: \n191: <!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n192: ## Documentation\n193: \n194: - [ ] CHK-040 [P1] `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `implementation-summary.md` state the same bullet text, byte count and pin count.\n195: - [ ] CHK-041 [P1] `HOOKDOC` names seven adapters and holds the invocation table (T005, T018).\n196: - [ ] CHK-042 [P2] The runtime-mirrors README names both pointer blocks (T021).\n197: <!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n198: \n199: ---\n200: \n201: <!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n202: ## File Organization\n203: \n204: - [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Probes, before and after output live in `scratch/` only.\n205: - [ ] CHK-051 [P1] `scratch/` holds only the evidence files the summary cites at completion.\n206: <!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n207: \n208: ---\n209: \n210: <!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n211: ## Verification Summary\n212: \n213: | Category | Total | Verified |\n214: |----------|-------|----------|\n215: | P0 Items | 13 | 1/13 |\n216: | P1 Items | 12 | 0/12 |\n217: | P2 Items | 1 | 0/1 |\n218: \n219: **Verification Date**: 2026-11-12\n220: <!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n221: \n222: ---","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/tasks.md, lines 1-222\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Tasks: Phase 6: gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers\"\n3: description: \"Ordered tasks to add the Gate 2 command bullet, copy it into the Cursor rule, hand hub modes to their commands, name the plan workflow at Gate 3 and downgrade commands in a child brief.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"gate 2 binding and runtime pointers tasks\"\n6: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7: contextType: \"general\"\n8: ---\n9: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n10: # Tasks: Phase 6: gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers\n11: \n12: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n17: ## Task Notation\n18: \n19: | Prefix | Meaning |\n20: |--------|---------|\n21: | `[ ]` | Pending |\n22: | `[x]` | Completed |\n23: | `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n24: | `[B]` | Blocked |\n25: \n26: **Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n27: \n28: Every command runs from the repository root unless a task says otherwise. `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`. `SSK` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime`. `SYNC` is `$SSK/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs`. `MAN` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json`. `CHK` is `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs`. `HOOKDOC` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`. `S` is this phase's `scratch/` folder. `G1T` is `(cd $SSK/cli && npx vitest run tests/gate1-pointer-sync.vitest.ts --config ../vitest.config.ts --root .)`.\n29: \n30: Each task is one change to the files it names, small enough for a worker with a short brief. The operator answered the four wording questions on 2026-11-12, and `spec.md` section 10 quotes each answer. No task reads holdout prompt text.\n31: \n32: Worker waves. Tasks in one wave touch different files and can run in parallel.\n33: - Wave 0, 2 tasks: T001, T002. Read-only setup.\n34: - Wave 1, 12 tasks: T003 (`AGENTS.md`), T004 (`SYNC`), T005 (`HOOKDOC`), T006 (`advisor-runtime-values.ts`), T007 (`advisor-observability.vitest.ts`), T008 (`hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts`), T009, T010 and T011 (one `ROUTER.md` each), T012 (`spec-gate-core.mjs`), T013 (`create.sh`), T014 (the deriver, only if its condition holds).\n35: - Wave 2, 8 tasks: T015 (`render.ts`), T016 (`MAN`), T017 (gate1 test), T018 (`HOOKDOC`), T019 (parity test, new), T020 (spec-gate test), T021 (runtime-mirrors README), T022 (label removal test, new).\n36: - Wave 3, 4 tasks: T023 (child render test, new), T024 (`MAN`, generated), T025 (`.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md`, generated), T026 (`HOOKDOC`).\n37: - Verification, 9 tasks, one at a time: T027 to T035.\n38: <!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n39: \n40: ---\n41: \n42: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n43: ## Phase 1: Setup\n44: \n45: - [x] T001 Re-read the before numbers (`$S/before.txt`). Verify: `$CHK | grep -E \"^A(4|6) |^STATUS\"` prints `44 current`, `15629 of 16384` and `STATUS=OK`, `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-manifest.cjs --check` prints `30 pins`, `node $SYNC --check` exits 0 and `node $S/measure-policies.mjs | head -1` prints `commands 44 {\"start\":20,\"ask\":17,\"run\":7}`.\n46: - [x] T002 Confirm phase 005 shipped the brief line (`$S/phase005-check.txt`). Verify: `bash $S/hook-first-line.sh \"create a readme for the utils folder\"` prints a line holding `/create:readme` and `(start)`. If it does not, mark T014, T015, T023, T026 and T033 `[B]` with the line it printed, and carry on with the rest.\n47: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n48: \n49: ---\n50: \n51: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n52: ## Phase 2: Implementation\n53: \n54: - [x] T003 Insert one line in `AGENTS.md` Gate 2, right after the line `- Confidence ≥ 0.8 → MUST invoke skill | < 0.8 → general approach | User names skill → cite and proceed`. The line is the exact content of `$S/bullet-draft.txt`: ``- **Command in the brief.** A brief or advisor result that names a command offers its workflow beside the skill's. Take either path whole, never an improvised one. To take the command, read its document in full and follow it. `run` starts it now. `start` starts it without `:auto`, so its setup asks. `ask` offers it in one question and waits. A typed command or explicit instruction outranks the policy. Output: `COMMAND: [/name] → [started|offered|declined]` `` (`AGENTS.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"^- \\*\\*Command in the brief\\.\\*\\*\" AGENTS.md` prints 1, and `diff <(rg \"^- \\*\\*Command in the brief\" AGENTS.md) $S/bullet-draft.txt` prints nothing.\n55: - [x] T004 In `SYNC`, add a second block. Add the constants `START_COMMAND = '<!-- spec-kit:gate2-command-pointer:start -->'`, `END_COMMAND = '<!-- spec-kit:gate2-command-pointer:end -->'`, `GATE_TWO_CALL_MARKER = 'skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend'` and `GATE_TWO_COMMAND_MARKER = '**Command in the brief.**'`. Read the first `AGENTS.md` line holding each marker, with a leading `2. ` stripped as `readGateOneLine` does. When both lines exist, write a block right after the Gate 1 block: the start marker, `## Gate 2 command routing (generated from the root AGENTS.md)`, a blank line, `Cursor gets no per-prompt advisor brief under the tested build. Before acting, run the direct call below, then apply the command rule:`, a blank line, the call line, a blank line, the command line, a blank line, the same `Generated by` line as block one, the end marker. When either line is missing, remove an existing second block and write nothing for it. Under `--check`, report `pointer block differs from the root AGENTS.md Gate 2 lines` or `no Gate 2 command block` and exit 1. Export the new names (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs`). Verify: `node --check $SYNC` exits 0, and `rg -c \"GATE_TWO_COMMAND_MARKER = '\\*\\*Command in the brief\\.\\*\\*'\" $SYNC` prints 1.\n56: - [x] T005 [P] In `HOOKDOC` section 3, add a DSH row after the OpenCode row: runtime `**DSH**`, adapter `system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs`, imported by `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/prompt-advisor.mjs`, wiring `agent/pre-step` through the `repo-guards` plugin, on unless the `promptAdvisor` row flag is `false`, payload note `A fan-out leaf, marked by the lineage patch, gets no brief`, delivery `Brief added to the step`. In section 4, add a `dsh/` entry with `README.md` and `prompt-advisor.mjs` (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`). Verify: `rg -n '^\\| \\*\\*DSH\\*\\* \\|' $HOOKDOC` prints 1 line, and `rg -c \"prompt-advisor.mjs\" $HOOKDOC` prints at least 2.\n57: - [x] T006 [P] Remove the `'copilot',` line from `ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES`, leaving seven labels in this order: `claude`, `opencode`, `pi`, `codex`, `cursor`, `devin`, `dsh`. Add no retired list (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/advisor-runtime-values.ts`). Verify: `rg -c \"copilot\" $ADV/lib/advisor-runtime-values.ts` prints nothing and exits 1, and in `$ADV`, `npm run typecheck` exits 0.\n58: - [x] T007 [P] In the observability test, change the expectation `expect(ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES).toEqual([...])` to the seven labels T006 leaves, in the same order (`$ADV/tests/legacy/advisor-observability.vitest.ts`). Verify: after T006, in `$ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/legacy/advisor-observability.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, and `rg -c \"copilot\" $ADV/tests/legacy/advisor-observability.vitest.ts` prints nothing.\n59: - [x] T008 [P] In the brief benchmark, delete the `copilot` row of `SEVEN_AXIS_MATRIX` and drop `copilot` from the header comment that lists the runtimes (`$ADV/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts`). Verify: `rg -c \"copilot\" $ADV/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts` prints nothing and exits 1. The bench sits outside `npm run typecheck` and the default test run, so this grep is its check.\n60: - [x] T009 [P] Add one bullet as the last item of section 4, HOW TO READ THIS, in `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md`: ``- A mode whose `mode-registry.json` row names a `command` has two whole entries: read that command's document in full and follow it under the policy the advisor names, or follow this mode's packet. Pick one and keep to it. A mode whose row has `command: null` has only its packet.`` (`.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"has two whole entries\" .skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md` prints 1, and `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/sk-doc` exits 0.\n61: - [x] T010 [P] Add the same bullet as T009 as the last item of section 4 in `.skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md` (`.skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"has two whole entries\" .skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md` prints 1, and `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/sk-design` exits 0.\n62: - [x] T011 [P] Add the T009 bullet as the last item of section 4 in `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/ROUTER.md`, followed in the same bullet by: ``Where a mode packet names its command as its only entry, as `deep-research/SKILL.md` does, both entries lead to the command.`` (`.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/ROUTER.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"has two whole entries\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/ROUTER.md` prints 1, and `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop` exits 0.\n63: - [x] T012 [P] In `GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE`, insert one array item right after `'The answer holds for the rest of this session: do not ask this again on later turns.'`: `'For a new folder, start /speckit:plan, or /speckit:complete when the operator asked for the build itself: read that command document in full and follow it without :auto.'` (`$SSK/hooks/lib/spec-gate/spec-gate-core.mjs`). Verify: `rg -c \"speckit:plan\" $SSK/hooks/lib/spec-gate/spec-gate-core.mjs` prints 1, and `node --check $SSK/hooks/lib/spec-gate/spec-gate-core.mjs` exits 0.\n64: - [x] T013 [P] In the standard next-steps block of `create.sh`, the one that prints `1. Fill out spec.md with requirements`, add after the lazy add-ons `if` block: `echo \"    6. Plan the work with /speckit:plan, or plan and build with /speckit:complete, unless one of them created this folder\"` (`$SSK/cli/spec/create.sh`). Verify: `bash -n $SSK/cli/spec/create.sh` exits 0, and `rg -c \"6. Plan the work with /speckit:plan\" $SSK/cli/spec/create.sh` prints 1.\n65: - [x] T014 The command table phase 005 generates (`COMMAND_ROWS` in `$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`) carries a policy but no `mutating` class, and T015 needs the class. In `renderCommandRows` of `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs`, add `mutating: '<class>'` to each `COMMAND_ROWS` row, taken from the same `commandPolicies` record that supplies the row's policy, placed after `policy` and left out when the row has no policy record. In `$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`, add `readonly mutating?: 'read-only' | 'add-only' | 'mutates';` to the `CommandRow` interface, outside the generated block. Then run `node $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs`. Verify: `node $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs --check | jq -r .status` prints `fresh`, `rg -c \"'command-doctor-git-setup': \\{ command: '/doctor:git setup', policy: 'run', mutating: 'read-only'\" $ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` prints 1, `rg -c \"'command-doctor-speckit': \\{ command: '/doctor:speckit', policy: 'run', mutating: 'add-only'\" $ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` prints 1, and in `$ADV`, `npm run typecheck` exits 0 and `npx vitest run tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts tests/doctor-command-bridges.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n66: - [ ] T015 In `$ADV/lib/render.ts`, add `childSession?: boolean` to `AdvisorBriefRenderOptions`, defaulting to `process.env.AI_SESSION_CHILD === '1'`. When it is true, the command shown in the head line, and in an `Also:` line, renders `(parent-named only)` in place of its policy word when the policy is `start` or `ask`, or when it is `run` and the class is not `read-only`. Nothing else in the brief changes (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV`, `npm run typecheck` exits 0, and `npx vitest run tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts tests/hooks` reports 0 failed.\n67: - [ ] T016 [P] In `MAN` `pins`, add an entry right after `gate1-lookup`: `\"id\": \"gate2-command\"`, `\"kind\": \"first-occurrence\"`, `\"section\": \"gate-2\"`, `\"texts\": [\"**Command in the brief.**\"]`, `\"consumer\": \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs\"`, `\"consumer_evidence\": [\"GATE_TWO_COMMAND_MARKER = '**Command in the brief.**'\"]` and a `why` saying the Cursor rule's second block is generated from the first line holding this marker (`.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json`). Verify: `node -e 'const m=require(\"./.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json\");console.log(m.pins.length, m.pins.some((p)=>p.id===\"gate2-command\"))'` prints `31 true`.\n68: - [ ] T017 [P] In `gate1-pointer-sync.vitest.ts`, seed `AGENTS.md` with a Gate 2 call line and a command line, and add three cases: both blocks are written and `--check` exits 0, a root with no command line gets block one only and a stale second block is removed, and a hand edit inside the second block makes `--check` exit 1 with `pointer block differs from the root AGENTS.md Gate 2 lines` (`$SSK/cli/tests/gate1-pointer-sync.vitest.ts`). Verify: `$G1T` reports 7 passed and 0 failed.\n69: - [ ] T018 [P] In `HOOKDOC`, add a subsection `### Starting a surfaced command` at the end of section 3. It says the command document is `.skilled/commands/<group>/<name>.md`, the model reads it in full and follows it on every runtime, never tells the user to type a slash command and asks the user to type one only when it cannot read the file. Then a table with columns `Runtime`, `Model can start a command itself` and `Basis`, one row each for Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Devin, Pi, OpenCode and DSH, taken from section 2.8 of `../../007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/synthesis-review.md`. Write runtime names in plain text, not bold, so the parity test reads only the adapter table. Claude Code's row says the Skill tool is a shortcut for the names it lists, and that it lists one `create` entry and none of the other twelve `create:*` names (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`). Verify: `rg -n \"^### Starting a surfaced command\" $HOOKDOC` prints 1 line, and `rg -c '^\\| \\*\\*' $HOOKDOC` still prints 7.\n70: - [ ] T019 [P] Create `$ADV/tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts`. Export a pure `compareRuntimeLists(index, table, enumValues)` that returns the names missing from each list. Read the index as the directory names under `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/`, the table as the lowercased bold names in `HOOKDOC` rows matching `^\\| \\*\\*([A-Za-z]+)\\*\\* \\|`, and the enum as `ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES`. One case asserts the three real lists agree. One case passes an index with an extra name and asserts the function reports it (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts` reports 2 passed and 0 failed.\n71: - [ ] T020 [P] In the test `Gate-3 delivery flag off preserves byte-identical baseline output`, add the T012 line to the `mutationNotice` array at the same position (`$SSK/tests/hooks/spec-gate-core.test.mjs`). Verify: `(cd $SSK && node --test tests/hooks/spec-gate-core.test.mjs)` prints `fail 0` and `pass 107`.\n72: - [ ] T021 [P] In the `sync-gate1-pointers.cjs` row of the runtime-mirrors README, say the script writes two blocks into `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md`: the Gate 1 lookup and the Gate 2 command rule with its direct call (`$SSK/cli/runtime-mirrors/README.md`). Verify: `rg -n \"sync-gate1-pointers\" $SSK/cli/runtime-mirrors/README.md` prints a line naming `Gate 2`.\n73: - [ ] T022 [P] Create `$ADV/tests/legacy/runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts` for a record or input that still carries `copilot`. Use a temporary workspace root and delete the two files it writes afterwards. Cases: a diagnostics file at `advisorHookDiagnosticsPath(root)` holding one valid `claude` record and one otherwise valid `copilot` record makes `readAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecords(root)` return only the `claude` record without throwing. The same holds for an outcomes file at `advisorHookOutcomesPath(root)` and `readAdvisorHookOutcomeRecords(root)`. `serializeAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord` throws for a `copilot` record. `validateSkillExecutionOutcomeRecord` returns false for one. `AdvisorValidateInputSchema.safeParse` fails for an `outcomeEvents` entry with `runtime: 'copilot'` and names that path in its issues (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/legacy/runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts`). Verify: after T006, in `$ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/legacy/runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts` reports 5 passed and 0 failed.\n74: - [ ] T023 [P] Create `$ADV/tests/render-child-session.vitest.ts`. Cases, each rendering one result through `renderAdvisorBrief`: child set and policy `start`, `ask`, `run` with `read-only` and `run` with `add-only`, then the variable set to `0` and unset. Expected: `(parent-named only)` for `start`, `ask` and `run` with `add-only`, the policy word for `run` with `read-only`, and output byte-equal to the non-child render for `0` and unset. One more case renders `/doctor:git hooks` as top with the child set (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/render-child-session.vitest.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/render-child-session.vitest.ts` reports 7 passed and 0 failed.\n75: - [ ] T024 Regenerate the manifest's derived copy (`MAN`). Verify: `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-manifest.cjs --write` exits 0, then `--check` prints `PASS: 44 sections, 31 pins, derived matches AGENTS.md`.\n76: - [ ] T025 [P] Regenerate the Cursor rule (`.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md`). Verify: `node $SYNC` exits 0, then `node $SYNC --check` exits 0, `rg -c \"Command in the brief\" .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` prints 1 and `rg -c \"skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend\" .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` prints 1.\n77: - [ ] T026 [P] In `HOOKDOC` section 2, step 5 Render, add one sentence: with `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` a surfaced `start` or `ask` command, or a `run` command that is not read-only, renders as `(parent-named only)` (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"parent-named only\" $HOOKDOC` prints 1.\n78: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n79: \n80: ---\n81: \n82: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n83: ## Phase 3: Verification\n84: \n85: - [ ] T027 Run the agents-md check (`$S/after-check.txt`). Verify: `$CHK` prints `STATUS=OK`, A4 `44 current`, A5 `31/31 pins hold`, A10 `6/6` and A6 at or under `16384`, expected `16092` with the T003 text unchanged.\n86: - [ ] T028 Run the rule-copy canary. Verify: `node .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/scripts/check-rule-copies.js | head -1` prints a line starting `OK: all rule invariants present`.\n87: - [ ] T029 Run the pointer test and check. Verify: `$G1T` reports 7 passed, and `node $SYNC --check` exits 0.\n88: - [ ] T030 Run the spec gate test. Verify: `(cd $SSK && node --test tests/hooks/spec-gate-core.test.mjs)` prints `fail 0`.\n89: - [ ] T031 Run the advisor checks. Verify: in `$ADV`, `npm run typecheck` exits 0, `npx vitest run tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts tests/render-child-session.vitest.ts tests/legacy/runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts tests/legacy/advisor-observability.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `rg -n \"copilot\" $ADV --glob \"*.ts\" --glob \"!dist/**\" --glob \"!node_modules/**\"` prints only the new test and the adapter-path guards in `tests/hooks/settings-driven-invocation-parity.vitest.ts` and `stress-test/skill-advisor/hooks-parity-stress.vitest.ts` and `npm test` reports 0 failed.\n90: - [ ] T032 Run the three hub checks. Verify: `for h in sk-doc sk-design system-deep-loop; do node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/$h > /dev/null 2>&1; echo \"$h exit=$?\"; done` prints `exit=0` three times.\n91: - [ ] T033 Rebuild the advisor and probe the hook. Verify: in `$ADV`, `npm run build` exits 0. Then `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1 bash $S/hook-first-line.sh \"disable comment hygiene gate\"` prints a line holding `/doctor:git hooks (parent-named only)`, and the same command without the variable prints the phase 005 line with its policy word.\n92: - [ ] T034 Check scope and comment hygiene. Verify: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --stat` names only files in `spec.md` section 3, and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff -U0 -- '*.ts' '*.cjs' '*.mjs' '*.sh' | rg \"^\\+.*(REQ-0|T0[0-9]{2}|specs/|ADR-)\"` prints nothing.\n93: - [ ] T035 Write `implementation-summary.md` and mark each row in `acceptance-criteria.md` with its evidence. Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <this folder> --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n94: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n95: \n96: ---\n97: \n98: <!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n99: ## Completion Criteria\n100: \n101: - [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n102: - [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n103: - [ ] `$CHK` prints `STATUS=OK` and `node $SYNC --check` exits 0 with the bullet in place\n104: <!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n105: \n106: ---\n107: \n108: <!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n109: ## Cross-References\n110: \n111: - **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n112: - **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n113: - **Acceptance criteria**: See `acceptance-criteria.md`\n114: - **Review**: `../../007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/synthesis-review.md` R5, R6, R10b, L4, L5, L10, G1 and G3\n115: <!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n116: \n117: ---\n118: \n119: ## Verification Checklist\n120: \n121: <!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n122: ## Verification Protocol\n123: \n124: | Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n125: |----------|----------|-------------------|\n126: | **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n127: | **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n128: | **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n129: \n130: A blocked task gets `[B]` and one line naming what blocks it. An A6 reading above 16384 blocks the phase.\n131: <!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n132: \n133: ---\n134: \n135: <!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n136: ## Pre-Implementation\n137: \n138: - [x] CHK-001 [P0] The four wording questions have an operator answer, quoted in `spec.md` section 10. Evidence: answered on 2026-11-12 through the question dialog. T003, T006, T012, T013, T015 and T026 follow those answers.\n139: - [ ] CHK-002 [P0] The before numbers are in `$S/before.txt` (T001).\n140: - [ ] CHK-003 [P1] Phase 005's brief line is confirmed, or the REQ-004 tasks are marked `[B]` (T002).\n141: <!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n142: \n143: ---\n144: \n145: <!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n146: ## Code Quality\n147: \n148: - [ ] CHK-010 [P0] In `$ADV`, `npm run typecheck` exits 0, and `node --check` exits 0 on `SYNC` and `spec-gate-core.mjs`.\n149: - [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No code comment names a spec path, a phase number, a requirement or a task id (T034).\n150: - [ ] CHK-012 [P1] `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` is written by `SYNC` only, never by hand (T025).\n151: - [ ] CHK-013 [P1] The child branch reads the class, never the policy word alone (T015, T023).\n152: <!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n153: \n154: ---\n155: \n156: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n157: ## Testing Checklist\n158: \n159: - [ ] CHK-020 [P0] `$CHK` prints `STATUS=OK` with A6 at or under 16384 (T027).\n160: - [ ] CHK-021 [P0] The pointer test passes 7 cases and `--check` exits 0 (T029).\n161: - [ ] CHK-022 [P0] The child render test covers every renderer axis in `plan.md` (T023).\n162: - [ ] CHK-023 [P1] The spec gate test, the parity test and `npm test` in `$ADV` report 0 failed (T030, T031).\n163: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n164: \n165: ---\n166: \n167: <!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n168: ## FIX ADDENDUM: FIX COMPLETENESS\n169: \n170: - [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] The gap is class `cross-consumer`: one rule, read by seven runtimes through four surfaces.\n171: - [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Every reader of the pointer generator is checked: `rg -l \"sync-gate1-pointers\" .skilled --glob '!**/node_modules/**' --glob '!**/dist/**'` lists only files this phase changed or confirmed unchanged in `plan.md`.\n172: - [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Every reader of `GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE` is checked: `rg -n \"GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE\" .skilled --glob '!**/dist/**'` lists the core, its test and the injection contract, which names it without quoting it.\n173: - [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P1] The matrix axes in `plan.md` are listed in the two test file headers.\n174: - [ ] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] The child test sets and restores `AI_SESSION_CHILD`, so no other test sees it.\n175: - [ ] CHK-FIX-006 [P1] Evidence names the commit it ran on.\n176: <!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n177: \n178: ---\n179: \n180: <!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n181: ## Security\n182: \n183: - [ ] CHK-030 [P0] A child never sees a bare `start` or `ask` command line (T023).\n184: - [ ] CHK-031 [P0] No changed file names `/local-skilled-alignment`: `rg -n \"local-skilled-alignment\" <changed files>` prints nothing.\n185: - [ ] CHK-032 [P1] The pointer block copies tracked `AGENTS.md` text only (T004).\n186: - [ ] CHK-033 [P0] A stored record carrying `copilot` is skipped by both readers without an error, and tool input carrying it is rejected (T022).\n187: <!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n188: \n189: ---\n190: \n191: <!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n192: ## Documentation\n193: \n194: - [ ] CHK-040 [P1] `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `implementation-summary.md` state the same bullet text, byte count and pin count.\n195: - [ ] CHK-041 [P1] `HOOKDOC` names seven adapters and holds the invocation table (T005, T018).\n196: - [ ] CHK-042 [P2] The runtime-mirrors README names both pointer blocks (T021).\n197: <!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n198: \n199: ---\n200: \n201: <!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n202: ## File Organization\n203: \n204: - [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Probes, before and after output live in `scratch/` only.\n205: - [ ] CHK-051 [P1] `scratch/` holds only the evidence files the summary cites at completion.\n206: <!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n207: \n208: ---\n209: \n210: <!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n211: ## Verification Summary\n212: \n213: | Category | Total | Verified |\n214: |----------|-------|----------|\n215: | P0 Items | 13 | 1/13 |\n216: | P1 Items | 12 | 0/12 |\n217: | P2 Items | 1 | 0/1 |\n218: \n219: **Verification Date**: 2026-11-12\n220: <!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n221: \n222: ---"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/tasks.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794532151618,"end":1794532152059}}}}
