t/runtime`. `SYNC` is `$SSK/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs`. `MAN` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agent...","title":"grep","metadata":{"metadata":{"matches":65,"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found 65 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/spec.md:\n  Line 109: $ AI_SESSION_CHILD=1 bash P6/scratch/hook-first-line.sh \"disable comment hygiene gate\"\n\n  Line 112: $ rg -n \"AI_SESSION_CHILD\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor --glob '!**/dist/**' --glob '!**/node_modules/**'\n\n  Line 229: - Render a surfaced `start` or `ask` command, or a `run` command that is not read-only, as `(parent-named only)` in a session with `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` (R10b).\n\n  Line 279: | REQ-004 | With `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1`, `renderAdvisorBrief` shows a surfaced `start` or `ask` command, and a `run` command whose class is not `read-only`, as `(parent-named only)`. Without the variable the brief is byte-equal to phase 005's output. |\n\n  Line 302: - **SC-003**: A child-session brief for `disable comment hygiene gate` shows `/doctor:git hooks (parent-named only)`, and the same prompt without the variable shows the phase 005 line.\n\n  Line 336: - **NFR-R02**: Any value of `AI_SESSION_CHILD` other than `1` renders the normal brief, the same reading as `isChildSession` in `spec-gate-core.mjs`.\n\n  Line 377: - How does a dispatched child see a surfaced command? Answer: \"Shown as parent-named only (Recommended)\". `start`, `ask` and a `run` command that is not read-only render as `(parent-named only)`.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/plan.md:\n  Line 109: | Manual | The Claude hook on one prompt with and without `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` | `scratch/hook-first-line.sh` |\n\n  Line 214: ### ADR-005: A child sees a surfaced command as parent-named only\n\n  Line 216: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"Shown as parent-named only (Recommended)\"\n\n  Line 220: **Decision**: With `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1`, a surfaced `start` or `ask` command, or a `run` command whose class is not `read-only`, renders as `(parent-named only)`. The class comes from `commandPolicies`.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/implementation-summary.md:\n  Line 52: When this phase is built, a command the advisor names will come with one rule on every runtime: read its document in full and follow it under its policy, or take the skill path whole. Cursor and Devin will carry that rule in their own rule file, a hub skill will name its mode's command, a new folder will name the plan workflow and a dispatched child will see a surfaced command only as parent-named.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/acceptance-criteria.md:\n  Line 57: | AC-004 | REQ-004 | Given `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1`, When a brief surfaces a `start` or `ask` command or an add-only `run` command, Then it renders `(parent-named only)`, and with the variable unset or `0` the brief is byte-equal to phase 005's | In `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/render-child-session.vitest.ts` reports 7 passed, and `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1 bash $S/hook-first-line.sh \"disable comment hygiene gate\"` prints `/doctor:git hooks (parent-named only)` | Unmet | - |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/tasks.md:\n  Line 66: - [ ] T015 In `$ADV/lib/render.ts`, add `childSession?: boolean` to `AdvisorBriefRenderOptions`, defaulting to `process.env.AI_SESSION_CHILD === '1'`. When it is true, the command shown in the head line, and in an `Also:` line, renders `(parent-named only)` in place of its policy word when the policy is `start` or `ask`, or when it is `run` and the class is not `read-only`. Nothing else in the brief changes (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV`, `npm run typecheck` exits 0, and `npx vitest run tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts tests/hooks` reports 0 failed.\n\n  Line 74: - [ ] T023 [P] Create `$ADV/tests/render-child-session.vitest.ts`. Cases, each rendering one result through `renderAdvisorBrief`: child set and policy `start`, `ask`, `run` with `read-only` and `run` with `add-only`, then the variable set to `0` and unset. Expected: `(parent-named only)` for `start`, `ask` and `run` with `add-only`, the policy word for `run` with `read-only`, and output byte-equal to the non-child render for `0` and unset. One more case renders `/doctor:git hooks` as top with the child set (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/render-child-session.vitest.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/render-child-session.vitest.ts` reports 7 passed and 0 failed.\n\n  Line 77: - [ ] T026 [P] In `HOOKDOC` section 2, step 5 Render, add one sentence: with `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` a surfaced `start` or `ask` command, or a `run` command that is not read-only, renders as `(parent-named only)` (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"parent-named only\" $HOOKDOC` prints 1.\n\n  Line 91: - [ ] T033 Rebuild the advisor and probe the hook. Verify: in `$ADV`, `npm run build` exits 0. Then `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1 bash $S/hook-first-line.sh \"disable comment hygiene gate\"` prints a line holding `/doctor:git hooks (parent-named only)`, and the same command without the variable prints the phase 005 line with its policy word.\n\n  Line 174: - [ ] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] The child test sets and restores `AI_SESSION_CHILD`, so no other test sees it.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/scratch/briefs/w1-T009.txt:\n  Line 7: You are a non-interactive dispatched worker. `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` and\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/scratch/briefs/w2-T022.txt:\n  Line 7: You are a non-interactive dispatched worker. `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` and\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/scratch/briefs/w2-T016.txt:\n  Line 7: You are a non-interactive dispatched worker. `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` and\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/scratch/logs/w2-T022.out:\n  Line 3: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1794532165241,\"sessionID\":\"ses_e2d8e50c3ffehRVVY2CEr5OH1A\",\"part\":{\"partID\":\"prt_1d273c43e002H42KAlTuNmbKf1\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_e2d8e50c3ffehRVVY2CEr5OH1A\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1d27381d2001iJ0ZcKHw3YEnoQ\",\"type\":\"tool\",\"id\":\"call_269290796c534885b00120ec\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/tasks.md\"},\"output\":\"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-