{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794532226556,"sessionID":"ses_e2d8e593affeqxRun8M4iooLPr","part":{"partID":"prt_1d274b2c9002g5T2oF81SdvrM1","sessionID":"ses_e2d8e593affeqxRun8M4iooLPr","messageID":"msg_1d2748b4e0016fJWHLFS11xNkB","type":"tool","id":"call_a8feda89dbb84f819e268b26","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n \"ADR-005|matrix|axis|axes|Render|render\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/plan.md | head -60","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"62:- **Child downgrade** (`render.ts`): without it a child sees `/doctor:git hooks`, an `ask` route, as a plain recommendation.\n83:| `renderAdvisorBrief` | One brief for parent and child | Update, child branch only | `render-child-session.vitest.ts` and the unchanged golden briefs |\n89:Matrix axes for the generator: bullet present or absent, block two present or absent, block two edited by hand or clean. Matrix axes for the label removal: stored diagnostics record, stored outcome record, new diagnostic record and tool input, each carrying `copilot`. Matrix axes for the renderer: child variable set to `1`, set to another value or unset, policy `run`, `start` or `ask`, class `read-only` or not. Every axis has one test row.\n97:Follow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. Setup re-reads the before numbers and checks that phase 005 shipped. Implementation edits the bullet, the generator, the routers, the notice, the hook reference, the runtime enum and the renderer, then regenerates the manifest and the Cursor rule. Verification runs the agents-md check, the manifest check, the canary, the pointer check, the three test suites, the hub checks and two live hook probes.\n107:| Unit | Pointer generator: both blocks, no bullet, hand edit. Renderer: the child matrix. Runtime list: index, table and enum | `gate1-pointer-sync.vitest.ts`, `render-child-session.vitest.ts`, `advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts` |\n122:| Operator answers to the four wording questions | Decision | Green: answered on 2026-11-12, ADR-001 and ADR-005 to ADR-007 | None |\n214:### ADR-005: A child sees a surfaced command as parent-named only\n220:**Decision**: With `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1`, a surfaced `start` or `ask` command, or a `run` command whose class is not `read-only`, renders as `(parent-named only)`. The class comes from `commandPolicies`.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"62:- **Child downgrade** (`render.ts`): without it a child sees `/doctor:git hooks`, an `ask` route, as a plain recommendation.\n83:| `renderAdvisorBrief` | One brief for parent and child | Update, child branch only | `render-child-session.vitest.ts` and the unchanged golden briefs |\n89:Matrix axes for the generator: bullet present or absent, block two present or absent, block two edited by hand or clean. Matrix axes for the label removal: stored diagnostics record, stored outcome record, new diagnostic record and tool input, each carrying `copilot`. Matrix axes for the renderer: child variable set to `1`, set to another value or unset, policy `run`, `start` or `ask`, class `read-only` or not. Every axis has one test row.\n97:Follow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. Setup re-reads the before numbers and checks that phase 005 shipped. Implementation edits the bullet, the generator, the routers, the notice, the hook reference, the runtime enum and the renderer, then regenerates the manifest and the Cursor rule. Verification runs the agents-md check, the manifest check, the canary, the pointer check, the three test suites, the hub checks and two live hook probes.\n107:| Unit | Pointer generator: both blocks, no bullet, hand edit. Renderer: the child matrix. Runtime list: index, table and enum | `gate1-pointer-sync.vitest.ts`, `render-child-session.vitest.ts`, `advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts` |\n122:| Operator answers to the four wording questions | Decision | Green: answered on 2026-11-12, ADR-001 and ADR-005 to ADR-007 | None |\n214:### ADR-005: A child sees a surfaced command as parent-named only\n220:**Decision**: With `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1`, a surfaced `start` or `ask` command, or a `run` command whose class is not `read-only`, renders as `(parent-named only)`. The class comes from `commandPolicies`.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"rg -n \\\"ADR-005|matrix|axis|axes|Render|render\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/plan.md | head -60\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794532225737,"end":1794532226556}}}}
