pped`).toBeNull();\n72:     }\n73:   });\n74: \n75:   it('fails open on parse failure across all 3 runtimes', async () => {\n76:     const buildBrief = vi.fn(async (): Promise<AdvisorHookResult> => ({\n77:       status: 'fail_open',\n78:       freshness: 'unavailable',\n79:       brief: null,\n80:       recommendations: [],\n81:       diagnostics: null,\n82:       metrics: { durationMs: 0, cacheHit: false, subprocessInvoked: false, retriesAttempted: 0, recommendationCount: 0, tokenCap: 80 },\n83:       generatedAt: new Date().toISOString(),\n84:       sharedPayload: null,\n85:     }));\n86: \n87:     for (const runtime of RUNTIMES) {\n88:       const result = await buildBrief('', {\n89:         runtime,\n90:         workspaceRoot: process.cwd(),\n91:       });\n92:       expect(result.status, `runtime ${runtime} should fail open`).toBe('fail_open');\n93:       expect(renderAdvisorBrief(result), `runtime ${runtime} fail_open brief`).toBeNull();\n94:     }\n95:   });\n96: \n97:   it('accepts opencode runtime tag in buildSkillAdvisorBrief options', async () => {\n98:     const prompt = 'implement OAuth login flow';\n99:     const result = await buildSkillAdvisorBrief(prompt, {\n100:       runtime: 'opencode',\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 101]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/hooks/runtime-parity.vitest.ts, lines 1-100\n1: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: // MODULE: Runtime Parity Tests — Advisor brief shape across runtimes\n3: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: // Asserts that buildSkillAdvisorBrief produces a consistent brief\n5: // shape regardless of the runtime tag (claude, opencode, opencode).\n6: // The brief is rendered via renderAdvisorBrief; the test verifies:\n7: //   