{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794532295446,"sessionID":"ses_e2d8e593affeqxRun8M4iooLPr","part":{"partID":"prt_1d275bdf7002HRDiSwlV7bAF1P","sessionID":"ses_e2d8e593affeqxRun8M4iooLPr","messageID":"msg_1d275b5af001tv0HHZxR52KEzE","type":"tool","id":"call_43a84a1aefe4475d923232eb","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/plan.md","offset":50,"limit":75},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/plan.md, lines 50-124\n50: <!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n51: ## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n52: \n53: ### Pattern\n54: One source, generated copies, pointers at the point of use.\n55: \n56: ### Key Components\n57: - **Gate 2 bullet** (`AGENTS.md`): without it no runtime has a rule for a surfaced command, because Gate 2 today says only \"Confidence ≥ 0.8 → MUST invoke skill\".\n58: - **Manifest pin and derived copy** (`agents-md-manifest.json`): without the regenerated copy A4 reads `edited` and A12 fails, and without the pin a template edit that drops the marker leaves the Cursor block silently unwritten.\n59: - **Second pointer block** (`sync-gate1-pointers.cjs`): without it Cursor and Devin, which read `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` on its own, never see the bullet. Cursor's brief is dormant, so this is its only copy.\n60: - **Router handoff** (three `ROUTER.md` files): without it the skill path ends at the mode packet and never names the command its registry row records.\n61: - **Gate 3 line** (`GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE`, `create.sh`): without it a plain build request gets the folder question and no workflow, because the advisor names no command for it (Measured Behavior).\n62: - **Child downgrade** (`render.ts`): without it a child sees `/doctor:git hooks`, an `ask` route, as a plain recommendation.\n63: - **Runtime parity test** (`advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts`): without it the hook reference drifts from the adapters again, as it did when DSH was added.\n64: \n65: ### Data Flow\n66: An operator edits the Gate 2 bullet. `agents-md-manifest.cjs --write` copies the new body into `derived`, and `sync-gate1-pointers.cjs` copies the direct-call line and the bullet into the Cursor rule. `/doctor:agents-md check` then reads the budget, the currency and the pointer drift in one run. At prompt time a brief or CLI result names a command, and the model reads that command's document, takes the skill path instead or offers the command, by its policy word.\n67: <!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n68: \n69: ---\n70: \n71: <!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n72: ## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n73: \n74: | Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n75: |---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n76: | `AGENTS.md` Gate 2 | Skill routing only | Update | `rg -c \"^- \\*\\*Command in the brief\\.\\*\\*\" AGENTS.md` prints 1 |\n77: | `agents-md-manifest.json` `pins` and `derived` | Pins 30 strings, copies 44 bodies | Update | `agents-md-manifest.cjs --check` prints 31 pins and `PASS` |\n78: | `agents-md-check.cjs` A10 | Runs the pointer generator's `--check` | Unchanged. It covers block two through the same exit code | A10 `PASS` |\n79: | `agents-md-embed.cjs` | Calls the pointer generator in a consumer repository | Unchanged. A consumer with no bullet gets block one only (NFR-R01) | Gate1 test case for a fixture with no bullet |\n80: | `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` | Gate 1 block, read by Cursor and Devin | Update by generator | `sync-gate1-pointers.cjs --check` exits 0 |\n81: | Hub `ROUTER.md` section 3 replay maps | Stage-two replay source | Unchanged. The bullet goes in section 4 | `parent-skill-check.cjs` exits 0 per hub |\n82: | `GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE` and `GATE_3_DENY_DETAIL` | Folder question at the first write, embedded in the deny text | Update. The deny text embeds the notice, so it changes with it | `spec-gate-core.test.mjs` 0 failed |\n83: | `renderAdvisorBrief` | One brief for parent and child | Update, child branch only | `render-child-session.vitest.ts` and the unchanged golden briefs |\n84: | `ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES` | Runtime enum for tool input, the CLI manifest and stored metrics records | Update: `copilot` removed | `advisor-observability.vitest.ts` expects seven labels |\n85: | `AdvisorValidateInputSchema` and the CLI manifest | Accept `outcomeEvents[].runtime` from the enum | Unchanged code. Input carrying `copilot` is now rejected | `runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts` |\n86: | `readAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecords`, `readAdvisorHookOutcomeRecords` | Filter stored lines through the record validators | Unchanged code. A stored `copilot` record is now skipped | `runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts` |\n87: | `hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts` | Fixture keyed by runtime | Update: the `copilot` row removed | `rg -c \"copilot\"` on the file prints nothing |\n88: \n89: Matrix axes for the generator: bullet present or absent, block two present or absent, block two edited by hand or clean. Matrix axes for the label removal: stored diagnostics record, stored outcome record, new diagnostic record and tool input, each carrying `copilot`. Matrix axes for the renderer: child variable set to `1`, set to another value or unset, policy `run`, `start` or `ask`, class `read-only` or not. Every axis has one test row.\n90: <!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n91: \n92: ---\n93: \n94: <!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n95: ## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n96: \n97: Follow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. Setup re-reads the before numbers and checks that phase 005 shipped. Implementation edits the bullet, the generator, the routers, the notice, the hook reference, the runtime enum and the renderer, then regenerates the manifest and the Cursor rule. Verification runs the agents-md check, the manifest check, the canary, the pointer check, the three test suites, the hub checks and two live hook probes.\n98: <!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n99: \n100: ---\n101: \n102: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n103: ## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n104: \n105: | Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n106: |-----------|-------|-------|\n107: | Unit | Pointer generator: both blocks, no bullet, hand edit. Renderer: the child matrix. Runtime list: index, table and enum | `gate1-pointer-sync.vitest.ts`, `render-child-session.vitest.ts`, `advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts` |\n108: | Integration | Delivery budget, section currency, pins, runtime copies and the canary over the real `AGENTS.md`. The pinned notice bytes | `agents-md-check.cjs`, `agents-md-manifest.cjs --check`, `check-rule-copies.js`, `spec-gate-core.test.mjs` |\n109: | Manual | The Claude hook on one prompt with and without `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` | `scratch/hook-first-line.sh` |\n110: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n111: \n112: ---\n113: \n114: <!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n115: ## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n116: \n117: | Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n118: |------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n119: | Phase 005 brief line `use <skill> → <command> (<policy>)` | Internal | Planned in parallel, not built | REQ-004 waits. Every other task proceeds |\n120: | Phase 002 `commandPolicies` with `mutating` on all 68 records | Internal | Green: in the generated file today | The child downgrade has no class to read |\n121: | Phase 003 `attachCommand` and the CLI `command` field | Internal | Code shipped, phase In Progress | The bullet binds to the brief only |\n122: | Operator answers to the four wording questions | Decision | Green: answered on 2026-11-12, ADR-001 and ADR-005 to ADR-007 | None |\n123: <!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n124: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 125]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/plan.md, lines 50-124\n50: <!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n51: ## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n52: \n53: ### Pattern\n54: One source, generated copies, pointers at the point of use.\n55: \n56: ### Key Components\n57: - **Gate 2 bullet** (`AGENTS.md`): without it no runtime has a rule for a surfaced command, because Gate 2 today says only \"Confidence ≥ 0.8 → MUST invoke skill\".\n58: - **Manifest pin and derived copy** (`agents-md-manifest.json`): without the regenerated copy A4 reads `edited` and A12 fails, and without the pin a template edit that drops the marker leaves the Cursor block silently unwritten.\n59: - **Second pointer block** (`sync-gate1-pointers.cjs`): without it Cursor and Devin, which read `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` on its own, never see the bullet. Cursor's brief is dormant, so this is its only copy.\n60: - **Router handoff** (three `ROUTER.md` files): without it the skill path ends at the mode packet and never names the command its registry row records.\n61: - **Gate 3 line** (`GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE`, `create.sh`): without it a plain build request gets the folder question and no workflow, because the advisor names no command for it (Measured Behavior).\n62: - **Child downgrade** (`render.ts`): without it a child sees `/doctor:git hooks`, an `ask` route, as a plain recommendation.\n63: - **Runtime parity test** (`advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts`): without it the hook reference drifts from the adapters again, as it did when DSH was added.\n64: \n65: ### Data Flow\n66: An operator edits the Gate 2 bullet. `agents-md-manifest.cjs --write` copies the new body into `derived`, and `sync-gate1-pointers.cjs` copies the direct-call line and the bullet into the Cursor rule. `/doctor:agents-md check` then reads the budget, the currency and the pointer drift in one run. At prompt time a brief or CLI result names a command, and the model reads that command's document, takes the skill path instead or offers the command, by its policy word.\n67: <!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n68: \n69: ---\n70: \n71: <!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n72: ## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n73: \n74: | Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n75: |---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n76: | `AGENTS.md` Gate 2 | Skill routing only | Update | `rg -c \"^- \\*\\*Command in the brief\\.\\*\\*\" AGENTS.md` prints 1 |\n77: | `agents-md-manifest.json` `pins` and `derived` | Pins 30 strings, copies 44 bodies | Update | `agents-md-manifest.cjs --check` prints 31 pins and `PASS` |\n78: | `agents-md-check.cjs` A10 | Runs the pointer generator's `--check` | Unchanged. It covers block two through the same exit code | A10 `PASS` |\n79: | `agents-md-embed.cjs` | Calls the pointer generator in a consumer repository | Unchanged. A consumer with no bullet gets block one only (NFR-R01) | Gate1 test case for a fixture with no bullet |\n80: | `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` | Gate 1 block, read by Cursor and Devin | Update by generator | `sync-gate1-pointers.cjs --check` exits 0 |\n81: | Hub `ROUTER.md` section 3 replay maps | Stage-two replay source | Unchanged. The bullet goes in section 4 | `parent-skill-check.cjs` exits 0 per hub |\n82: | `GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE` and `GATE_3_DENY_DETAIL` | Folder question at the first write, embedded in the deny text | Update. The deny text embeds the notice, so it changes with it | `spec-gate-core.test.mjs` 0 failed |\n83: | `renderAdvisorBrief` | One brief for parent and child | Update, child branch only | `render-child-session.vitest.ts` and the unchanged golden briefs |\n84: | `ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES` | Runtime enum for tool input, the CLI manifest and stored metrics records | Update: `copilot` removed | `advisor-observability.vitest.ts` expects seven labels |\n85: | `AdvisorValidateInputSchema` and the CLI manifest | Accept `outcomeEvents[].runtime` from the enum | Unchanged code. Input carrying `copilot` is now rejected | `runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts` |\n86: | `readAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecords`, `readAdvisorHookOutcomeRecords` | Filter stored lines through the record validators | Unchanged code. A stored `copilot` record is now skipped | `runtime-label-removal.vitest.ts` |\n87: | `hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts` | Fixture keyed by runtime | Update: the `copilot` row removed | `rg -c \"copilot\"` on the file prints nothing |\n88: \n89: Matrix axes for the generator: bullet present or absent, block two present or absent, block two edited by hand or clean. Matrix axes for the label removal: stored diagnostics record, stored outcome record, new diagnostic record and tool input, each carrying `copilot`. Matrix axes for the renderer: child variable set to `1`, set to another value or unset, policy `run`, `start` or `ask`, class `read-only` or not. Every axis has one test row.\n90: <!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n91: \n92: ---\n93: \n94: <!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n95: ## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n96: \n97: Follow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. Setup re-reads the before numbers and checks that phase 005 shipped. Implementation edits the bullet, the generator, the routers, the notice, the hook reference, the runtime enum and the renderer, then regenerates the manifest and the Cursor rule. Verification runs the agents-md check, the manifest check, the canary, the pointer check, the three test suites, the hub checks and two live hook probes.\n98: <!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n99: \n100: ---\n101: \n102: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n103: ## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n104: \n105: | Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n106: |-----------|-------|-------|\n107: | Unit | Pointer generator: both blocks, no bullet, hand edit. Renderer: the child matrix. Runtime list: index, table and enum | `gate1-pointer-sync.vitest.ts`, `render-child-session.vitest.ts`, `advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts` |\n108: | Integration | Delivery budget, section currency, pins, runtime copies and the canary over the real `AGENTS.md`. The pinned notice bytes | `agents-md-check.cjs`, `agents-md-manifest.cjs --check`, `check-rule-copies.js`, `spec-gate-core.test.mjs` |\n109: | Manual | The Claude hook on one prompt with and without `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` | `scratch/hook-first-line.sh` |\n110: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n111: \n112: ---\n113: \n114: <!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n115: ## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n116: \n117: | Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n118: |------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n119: | Phase 005 brief line `use <skill> → <command> (<policy>)` | Internal | Planned in parallel, not built | REQ-004 waits. Every other task proceeds |\n120: | Phase 002 `commandPolicies` with `mutating` on all 68 records | Internal | Green: in the generated file today | The child downgrade has no class to read |\n121: | Phase 003 `attachCommand` and the CLI `command` field | Internal | Code shipped, phase In Progress | The bullet binds to the brief only |\n122: | Operator answers to the four wording questions | Decision | Green: answered on 2026-11-12, ADR-001 and ADR-005 to ADR-007 | None |\n123: <!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n124: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 125]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/plan.md\",\"offset\":50,\"limit\":75}"},"time":{"start":1794532294135,"end":1794532295446}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794532295453,"sessionID":"ses_e2d8e593affeqxRun8M4iooLPr","part":{"partID":"prt_1d275c083001GrXgoR7lbGcBCU","sessionID":"ses_e2d8e593affeqxRun8M4iooLPr","messageID":"msg_1d275b5af001tv0HHZxR52KEzE","type":"tool","id":"call_687751414eae452481ecdf46","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/plan.md","offset":205,"limit":40},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/plan.md, lines 205-244\n205: **Context**: `/local-skilled-alignment` is private and untracked.\n206: \n207: **Decision**: No surface in this phase names it.\n208: \n209: **Consequences**:\n210: - `rg -n \"local-skilled-alignment\"` over the changed files prints nothing.\n211: \n212: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n213: - A local overlay: rejected by the operator (Q012).\n214: ### ADR-005: A child sees a surfaced command as parent-named only\n215: \n216: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"Shown as parent-named only (Recommended)\"\n217: \n218: **Context**: A child session gets the same brief as its parent. In this worktree a child got `/doctor:git hooks`, an `ask` route, as a plain recommendation.\n219: \n220: **Decision**: With `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1`, a surfaced `start` or `ask` command, or a `run` command whose class is not `read-only`, renders as `(parent-named only)`. The class comes from `commandPolicies`.\n221: \n222: **Consequences**:\n223: - A child still sees the skill line and a read-only command.\n224: \n225: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n226: - Drop the command from a child's brief, or send a child no brief: the operator chose the downgrade.\n227: \n228: ### ADR-006: The Gate 3 notice names the plan workflow for a new folder\n229: \n230: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"/speckit:plan, or /speckit:complete for a build (Recommended)\"\n231: \n232: **Context**: A plain build request gets no command from the advisor, so the first write meets the folder question and no workflow.\n233: \n234: **Decision**: The notice and the standard `create.sh` next steps name `/speckit:plan`, or `/speckit:complete` when the operator asked for the build itself.\n235: \n236: **Consequences**:\n237: - The pinned notice test changes in the same task wave.\n238: \n239: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n240: - `/speckit:plan` only, or both with no preference.\n241: \n242: ### ADR-007: `copilot` is removed from the runtime enum\n243: \n244: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"Drop it\": \"The label is removed. Old stored records and any tool input carrying 'copilot' fail validation from then on.\"\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 245]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/plan.md, lines 205-244\n205: **Context**: `/local-skilled-alignment` is private and untracked.\n206: \n207: **Decision**: No surface in this phase names it.\n208: \n209: **Consequences**:\n210: - `rg -n \"local-skilled-alignment\"` over the changed files prints nothing.\n211: \n212: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n213: - A local overlay: rejected by the operator (Q012).\n214: ### ADR-005: A child sees a surfaced command as parent-named only\n215: \n216: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"Shown as parent-named only (Recommended)\"\n217: \n218: **Context**: A child session gets the same brief as its parent. In this worktree a child got `/doctor:git hooks`, an `ask` route, as a plain recommendation.\n219: \n220: **Decision**: With `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1`, a surfaced `start` or `ask` command, or a `run` command whose class is not `read-only`, renders as `(parent-named only)`. The class comes from `commandPolicies`.\n221: \n222: **Consequences**:\n223: - A child still sees the skill line and a read-only command.\n224: \n225: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n226: - Drop the command from a child's brief, or send a child no brief: the operator chose the downgrade.\n227: \n228: ### ADR-006: The Gate 3 notice names the plan workflow for a new folder\n229: \n230: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"/speckit:plan, or /speckit:complete for a build (Recommended)\"\n231: \n232: **Context**: A plain build request gets no command from the advisor, so the first write meets the folder question and no workflow.\n233: \n234: **Decision**: The notice and the standard `create.sh` next steps name `/speckit:plan`, or `/speckit:complete` when the operator asked for the build itself.\n235: \n236: **Consequences**:\n237: - The pinned notice test changes in the same task wave.\n238: \n239: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n240: - `/speckit:plan` only, or both with no preference.\n241: \n242: ### ADR-007: `copilot` is removed from the runtime enum\n243: \n244: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"Drop it\": \"The label is removed. Old stored records and any tool input carrying 'copilot' fail validation from then on.\"\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 245]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/plan.md\",\"offset\":205,\"limit\":40}"},"time":{"start":1794532294787,"end":1794532295453}}}}
