{"type":"text","timestamp":1794532521414,"sessionID":"ses_e2d8e593affeqxRun8M4iooLPr","part":{"id":"prt_1d27925ae0024x53sREe0lp0XK","sessionID":"ses_e2d8e593affeqxRun8M4iooLPr","messageID":"msg_1d2791c6c001HJIuRkGmuqRwHt","type":"text","text":"T015 is implemented in `render.ts`. `childSession` resolves from `options.childSession`, falling back to `AI_SESSION_CHILD === '1'`, and the head and `Also:` command labels replace the policy word with `(parent-named only)` for `start`, `ask`, and non-read-only `run`.\n\nFiles written:\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts`\n\nVerify output, from `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`:\n\n```\n$ npm run typecheck\n> ../../system-spec-kit/node_modules/.bin/tsc --noEmit --composite false -p tsconfig.build.json\ntypecheck exit=0\n\n$ env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts tests/hooks\n Test Files  11 passed (11)\n      Tests  157 passed (157)\n   Duration  5.50s\n```\n\nThe env strip is required for this worker only. The harness sets `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1`, so the unchanged parent-behavior assertion in `tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts` sees `(parent-named only)` instead of `(start)`. Run as-is it reports 156 passed and 1 failed, with that single expected mismatch. The repository itself strips the marker before spawning child runs at `scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:816`.\n\nManual probes confirm `ask` and `add-only` render `(parent-named only)`, `run` with `read-only` keeps `(run)`, and unset or `0` renders the original policy word.\n\nProbe results:\n- `/doctor:git hooks` with child set gives `sk-git → /doctor:git hooks (parent-named only)`\n- `/doctor:git setup` with child set gives `sk-git → /doctor:git setup (run)`\n- `/doctor:update` as companion with child set gives `Also: /doctor:update (parent-named only)`\n- unset gives `sk-git → /doctor:git hooks (ask)`\n\nNothing was left undone in T015. The checkbox in `tasks.md` is untouched as instructed. The `Also:` line carries no policy word in the current renderer, so the marker is appended there and parent output stays byte-equal.","time":{"start":1794532517294,"end":1794532521414}}}
